{"id":"CVE-2005-1247","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2005-04-25T04:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T21:44:06.293Z","description":"webadmin.exe in Novell Nsure Audit 1.0.1 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service via malformed ASN.1 packets in corrupt client certificates to an SSL server, as demonstrated using an exploit for the OpenSSL ASN.1 parsing vulnerability.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.derkeiler.com/Mailing-Lists/securityfocus/bugtraq/2004-01/0126.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20040115 OpenSSL ASN.1 parsing bugs PoC / brute forcer"},{"url":"http://archives.neohapsis.com/archives/vulnwatch/2005-q2/0021.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_VULNWATCH"],"name":"20050424 [CIRT.DK - Advisory] Novell Nsure Audit 1.0.1 Denial of Service"},{"url":"http://www.cirt.dk/advisories/cirt-31-advisory.pdf","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://support.novell.com/cgi-bin/search/searchtid.cgi?/10097379.htm","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["openssl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2005-1730","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2007-03-03T23:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T21:59:24.289Z","description":"Multiple vulnerabilities in the OpenSSL ASN.1 parser, as used in Novell iManager 2.0.2, allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (NULL pointer dereference) via crafted packets, as demonstrated by \"OpenSSL ASN.1 brute forcer.\"  NOTE: this issue might overlap CVE-2004-0079, CVE-2004-0081, or CVE-2004-0112.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2005/0744","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2005-0744"},{"url":"http://www.cirt.dk/advisories/cirt-32-advisory.pdf","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/8732","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"8732"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/data/vulnerabilities/exploits/ASN.1-Brute.c","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["openssl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2005-2531","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2005-08-24T04:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T22:30:01.294Z","description":"OpenVPN before 2.0.1, when running with \"verb 0\" and without TLS authentication, does not properly flush the OpenSSL error queue when a client fails certificate authentication to the server and causes the error to be processed by the wrong client, which allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (client disconnection) via a large number of failed authentication attempts.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/14605","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"14605"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/17103","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"17103"},{"url":"http://openvpn.net/changelog.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.mandriva.com/security/advisories?name=MDKSA-2005:145","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_MANDRIVA"],"name":"MDKSA-2005:145"},{"url":"http://www.novell.com/linux/security/advisories/2005_20_sr.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"SUSE-SR:2005:020"},{"url":"http://www.debian.org/security/2005/dsa-851","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-851"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/16463","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"16463"}],"vendors":["openssl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2005-2532","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2005-08-24T04:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T22:30:01.155Z","description":"OpenVPN before 2.0.1 does not properly flush the OpenSSL error queue when a packet can not be decrypted by the server, which allows remote authenticated attackers to cause a denial of service (client disconnection) via a large number of packets that can not be decrypted.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/17103","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"17103"},{"url":"http://openvpn.net/changelog.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.mandriva.com/security/advisories?name=MDKSA-2005:145","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_MANDRIVA"],"name":"MDKSA-2005:145"},{"url":"http://www.debian.org/security/2005/dsa-851","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-851"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/14607","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"14607"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/16463","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"16463"}],"vendors":["openssl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2005-2946","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2005-09-16T04:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T22:53:29.917Z","description":"The default configuration on OpenSSL before 0.9.8 uses MD5 for creating message digests instead of a more cryptographically strong algorithm, which makes it easier for remote attackers to forge certificates with a valid certificate authority signature.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://bugzilla.ubuntu.com/show_bug.cgi?id=13593","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.ubuntu.com/usn/usn-179-1","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-179-1"},{"url":"http://www.cits.rub.de/MD5Collisions/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["openssl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2005-2969","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2005-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T22:53:29.946Z","description":"The SSL/TLS server implementation in OpenSSL 0.9.7 before 0.9.7h and 0.9.8 before 0.9.8a, when using the SSL_OP_MSIE_SSLV2_RSA_PADDING option, disables a verification step that is required for preventing protocol version rollback attacks, which allows remote attackers to force a client and server to use a weaker protocol than needed via a man-in-the-middle attack.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/17259","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"17259"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/23915","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"23915"},{"url":"http://www.novell.com/linux/security/advisories/2005_61_openssl.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"SUSE-SA:2005:061"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/26893","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"26893"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/17389","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"17389"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2005/3056","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2005-3056"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2007/2457","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2007-2457"},{"url":"http://support.avaya.com/elmodocs2/security/ASA-2006-260.htm","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/17813","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"17813"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/15071","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"15071"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/18165","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"18165"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/23340","tags":["third-party-advi